.echo === HD successor soak extra: slot-anchored pan steps and newline-terminated debug strings ===
.echo Harness-only hidden-desktop probe for the approved_hidden_cdb_host_soak class on the map-pan
.echo route, which loads slot __LOAD_SLOT__. It repeats the pan-press extra's press, re-arm and release
.echo breakpoints unchanged and adds two fixes for the long pan routes.
.echo First, the soak restarts each ten-second interval at the redraw that found a step due, so every
.echo step drifts by up to one redraw and the drift adds up: two hours of 720 intervals logged 716 to
.echo 719 steps as the redraw rate fell, under a floor of 718. When this probe takes a step over at
.echo 00406FA2 it moves the soak's own last-pan tick 00400054 back to the step's slot, which is the
.echo logged tick of the step before plus 640 ticks, so the next interval starts at the slot and no
.echo drift adds up. It does so only when all of these hold - the redraw came no more than 128 ticks
.echo after the slot, which is the legacy grader's two-second allowance - that redraw printed no
.echo heartbeat, whose row carries the redraw tick and must not follow a later tick - and this probe
.echo also took over the step before, so its slot is current. Otherwise the soak's redraw tick stays,
.echo the next slot counts from it, and one of at most 32 logged rows records the soak step, the step
.echo this probe expected, the heartbeat flag, the lateness and a running count. A late step
.echo therefore still widens its logged interval, and the replay grades every interval with the
.echo legacy periodic coverage rule. The logged tick of a slotted step is its slot, at most 128
.echo ticks before its redraw. The probe writes only the soak extra's step state and last-pan tick
.echo and the arrow key bytes the soak itself drives - never the scroll fields or native variables.
.echo Second, the audio stack prints debugger strings that end without a newline. The next soak row
.echo then shared their log line and was lost, 78 rows in 14 retained runs. The debugger now stops at
.echo every debug string the game process prints and ends its line. Nothing is hidden - the strings
.echo stay in the log, each on its own line.
.echo Disclosed as pan_press=cdb_extra_pressed_soak_pan_key_until_taken with
.echo pan_schedule=cdb_extra_logged_pan_step_at_its_slot_within_128_ticks and
.echo debug_output=cdb_newline_after_each_debuggee_debug_string - never user input. No echoed line
.echo begins with a marker name.
.echo Scratch in PE header padding free in every candidate: 004003C0 total re-arms, 004003C4 soak step
.echo of the last re-arm, 004003C8 re-arms of that step, 004003CC logged re-arm rows, 004003D0 soak
.echo step expected at the next takeover, 004003D4 logged tick of the last step taken over, 004003D8
.echo steps logged at their slot, 004003DC steps left at their redraw tick, 004003E0 logged rows of
.echo those.
sxe -c ".echo; gc" out
ed 004003c0 0
ed 004003c4 0xffffffff
ed 004003c8 0
ed 004003cc 0
ed 004003d0 0
ed 004003d4 0
ed 004003d8 0
ed 004003dc 0
ed 004003e0 0
bp 00406FA2 ".if (poi(00400040) == 5) { ed 00400040 8; .if (poi(00400050) == 0) { ed 004003d0 0; ed 004003d4 poi(00400044) }; .if ((poi(004003d0) == poi(00400050)) & ((poi(00400048) & 0x7ff) != 0) & (poi(00400054) >= (poi(004003d4) + 0n640)) & (poi(00400054) <= (poi(004003d4) + 0n768))) { ed 00400054 (poi(004003d4) + 0n640); ed 004003d8 (poi(004003d8)+1) } .else { ed 004003dc (poi(004003dc)+1); .if (poi(004003e0) < 0n32) { ed 004003e0 (poi(004003e0)+1); .printf \"\\nHDPAN_TICK_KEPT step=%d expected=%d beat=%d late=%d count=%d\\n\", poi(00400050), poi(004003d0), ((poi(00400048) & 0x7ff) == 0), (poi(00400054) - poi(004003d4) - 0n640), poi(004003dc) } }; ed 004003d4 poi(00400054); ed 004003d0 (poi(00400050)+1) }; gc"
